Okay, now you got your answer.

1277
01:11:14.720 --> 01:11:16.660
Now you got your answer.

1278
01:11:16.660 --> 01:11:20.100
All you have to do now is number four,

1279
01:11:20.100 --> 01:11:25.100
go and choose the answer that reflects that feeling

1280
01:11:25.960 --> 01:11:27.420
or anything close.

1281
01:11:28.900 --> 01:11:33.820
Do not choose the answer that reflects their words.

1282
01:11:35.020 --> 01:11:38.140
Because these empty questions always have what I call

1283
01:11:38.140 --> 01:11:40.720
the sucker answer there.

1284
01:11:40.720 --> 01:11:42.100
It's an answer that's wrong,

1285
01:11:42.100 --> 01:11:44.820
but it's there to sucker you into answering it.

1286
01:11:44.820 --> 01:11:48.820
And what it will reflect is what the patient said,

1287
01:11:48.820 --> 01:11:51.860
but it will ignore what the patient felt.

1288
01:11:51.860 --> 01:11:54.180
You're supposed to pick the answer that reflects

1289
01:11:54.180 --> 01:11:58.180
what they felt and ignore what they said.

1290
01:11:59.500 --> 01:12:00.780
Did you hear that?

1291
01:12:00.780 --> 01:12:05.780
Empathy ignores what is said and goes with what is felt.

1292
01:12:07.700 --> 01:12:09.940
Don't get it switched around.

1293
01:12:11.100 --> 01:12:13.980
When people have a hard time answering empathy questions,

1294
01:12:14.020 --> 01:12:17.100
it's usually because they respond directly

1295
01:12:17.100 --> 01:12:21.140
to what the patient said rather than how the patient feels.

1296
01:12:21.140 --> 01:12:22.900
Do you remember when, I don't know your name,

1297
01:12:22.900 --> 01:12:25.420
but I said, you're a real Brinslavic?

1298
01:12:26.620 --> 01:12:29.360
If you respond to what they said, you'll say,

1299
01:12:29.360 --> 01:12:31.200
a Brinslavic?

1300
01:12:31.200 --> 01:12:32.720
But if you respond to how they feel,

1301
01:12:32.720 --> 01:12:34.940
you'll say, I see you're angry.

1302
01:12:34.940 --> 01:12:36.240
Do you see the difference?

1303
01:12:36.240 --> 01:12:39.860
Now I want you to do the next three questions,

1304
01:12:39.860 --> 01:12:43.340
practice questions, and I want you to use these rules.

1305
01:12:43.340 --> 01:12:46.060
Put yourself in the client's place.

1306
01:12:46.060 --> 01:12:49.300
Say the words as though you really meant them.

1307
01:12:49.300 --> 01:12:54.300
Ask yourself, how would I be feeling if I said these words,

1308
01:12:54.780 --> 01:12:57.300
pick the answer that reflects that feeling.

1309
01:12:57.300 --> 01:13:02.340
I also want you to identify at least one sucker answer

1310
01:13:02.340 --> 01:13:05.520
that overemphasizes what the patient said,

1311
01:13:05.520 --> 01:13:09.040
but missed how the patient was feeling.

1312
01:13:09.040 --> 01:13:11.220
So do that and then talk to your buddy.

1313
01:13:13.340 --> 01:13:18.340
And stay on the task, I'll be right back.

1314
01:13:43.340 --> 01:13:44.180
Okay.

1315
01:14:13.340 --> 01:14:14.180
Okay.

1316
01:14:43.340 --> 01:14:44.180
Okay.

1317
01:15:13.340 --> 01:15:14.180
Okay.

1318
01:15:30.460 --> 01:15:31.980
So third one is really hard.

1319
01:15:34.160 --> 01:15:36.000
That third one, the problem with it is

1320
01:15:36.000 --> 01:15:38.400
when you put yourself in the patient's shoes

1321
01:15:38.400 --> 01:15:41.520
and say those words, no feeling really pops out.

1322
01:15:41.520 --> 01:15:44.260
So what you have to do is go to the answers

1323
01:15:44.260 --> 01:15:47.860
and see what feeling the answers are reflecting

1324
01:15:47.860 --> 01:15:51.900
and see which one has the best, the most likely feeling.

1325
01:15:51.900 --> 01:15:54.700
So go to your answers and see if you can get it that way.

1326
01:15:58.620 --> 01:16:00.620
Well, let me ask you about the first one.

1327
01:16:01.660 --> 01:16:04.420
She said, you're killers, you all killed my mother.

1328
01:16:06.260 --> 01:16:07.920
She died before I was born.

1329
01:16:08.860 --> 01:16:10.260
How does she feel?

1330
01:16:10.320 --> 01:16:13.200
You said those words and believe them, how would you feel?

1331
01:16:14.560 --> 01:16:15.720
Scared?

1332
01:16:15.720 --> 01:16:19.040
Okay, now go to the answers and find the answer

1333
01:16:19.040 --> 01:16:21.240
that reflects being scared.

1334
01:16:21.240 --> 01:16:22.840
Which one is it?

1335
01:16:22.840 --> 01:16:25.480
B, what is the sucker answer?

1336
01:16:25.480 --> 01:16:29.480
C, because that focused on what she said.

1337
01:16:29.480 --> 01:16:32.560
She isn't concerned about her mother.

1338
01:16:32.560 --> 01:16:34.480
She's scared.

1339
01:16:34.480 --> 01:16:35.800
She's frightened.

1340
01:16:35.800 --> 01:16:38.640
So the answer is B, the sucker answer is C.

1341
01:16:39.540 --> 01:16:41.680
The next one, what's the right answer?

1342
01:16:43.580 --> 01:16:47.580
D, and a sucker answer is any of the others.

1343
01:16:49.740 --> 01:16:52.540
Because the others focused on what he said.

1344
01:16:52.540 --> 01:16:54.420
D focused on how he feels.

1345
01:16:56.420 --> 01:16:59.700
Did anybody get an answer on the third one?

1346
01:16:59.700 --> 01:17:01.300
What did you say?

1347
01:17:01.300 --> 01:17:03.940
The answer is C, what's the sucker answer?

1348
01:17:05.260 --> 01:17:08.580
B, because B

1349
01:17:09.400 --> 01:17:10.560
says religious.

1350
01:17:10.560 --> 01:17:12.640
He's not feeling religious.

1351
01:17:12.640 --> 01:17:15.000
He's using a bunch of religious what?

1352
01:17:15.000 --> 01:17:15.920
Words.

1353
01:17:15.920 --> 01:17:18.260
That's the hint that it's the wrong answer.

1354
01:17:19.160 --> 01:17:21.960
He's feeling out of control.

1355
01:17:23.600 --> 01:17:26.400
So that's why C is the answer.

1356
01:17:26.400 --> 01:17:28.880
Because with those words, I can prove to you

1357
01:17:28.880 --> 01:17:30.340
that he has a control issue.

1358
01:17:30.340 --> 01:17:32.720
I can't prove to you that he feels religious.

1359
01:17:34.040 --> 01:17:35.200
So C is the right answer.

1360
01:17:35.200 --> 01:17:37.080
How many got C on that one?

1361
01:17:37.080 --> 01:17:38.040
Wow, that's great.

1362
01:17:38.040 --> 01:17:39.860
How many got all three?

1363
01:17:39.860 --> 01:17:40.700
Terrific.

1364
01:17:40.700 --> 01:17:43.620
If you missed any, do you see why you missed it?

1365
01:17:43.620 --> 01:17:45.540
What were some of the problems you had with that?

1366
01:17:45.540 --> 01:17:46.380
Anybody?

1367
01:17:47.820 --> 01:17:48.900
You've learned from it.

1368
01:17:48.900 --> 01:17:51.140
Any questions you have to give me about those?

1369
01:17:52.820 --> 01:17:54.420
Did you use the process?

1370
01:17:55.900 --> 01:17:57.180
Did the process help?

1371
01:17:58.100 --> 01:18:00.380
Okay, so that's what I want you to start doing.

1372
01:18:00.380 --> 01:18:03.460
I don't want you guessing on psych answers.

1373
01:18:03.460 --> 01:18:05.140
I want you to know the answer.

1374
01:18:05.140 --> 01:18:06.180
You understand what I'm saying?

1375
01:18:06.200 --> 01:18:09.600
So many times you guys just guess on psych answers.

1376
01:18:09.600 --> 01:18:12.840
I want you to know why you're picking what you're picking.

1377
01:18:12.840 --> 01:18:13.680
Okay.

1378
01:18:14.760 --> 01:18:16.600
Take a quick break.

1379
01:18:17.680 --> 01:18:20.360
Come back at 25 after.

1380
01:18:20.360 --> 01:18:22.500
And we'll just do the last lecture

1381
01:18:22.500 --> 01:18:24.580
and a wrap up and be done, okay?

1382
01:18:24.580 --> 01:18:27.480
And the sooner you're back, the sooner we'll get done.

1383
01:18:27.480 --> 01:18:28.320
Okay.
